From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satya Benson <satya@benson.earth>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:51:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: Fix invalid context in IOMFB parser KUnit
 test

iomfb_callback_envelope_test passes context 1 with a NULL packet header
to exercise invalid-context rejection. However, 1 is DCP_CONTEXT_ASYNC_CB,
so dcpep_handle_cb selects a valid channel and dereferences the NULL
header instead of rejecting the envelope.

Use DCP_NUM_CONTEXTS, the first out-of-range context, to exercise the
existing unknown-channel guard. This only corrects the test fixture;
production parser behavior is unchanged.

Fixes: 0871fb01d95b ("drm/apple: Test firmware message bounds with KUnit")
Signed-off-by: Satya Benson <satya@benson.earth>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit f9382a9201b0349429cbd8609f261fee54d7d17d)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb-parser-test.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb-parser-test.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb-parser-test.c
index e829ff43bd..31620a2be3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb-parser-test.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb-parser-test.c
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ static void iomfb_callback_envelope_test(struct kunit *test)
 		KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, dcp->ch_cb.depth, cases[i].depth);
 	}
 	dcp->crashed = false;
-	dcpep_handle_cb(dcp, 1, NULL, sizeof(struct dcp_packet_header), 0);
+	dcpep_handle_cb(dcp, DCP_NUM_CONTEXTS, NULL, sizeof(struct dcp_packet_header), 0);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, dcp->crashed);
 }
 
